/* These three were sized in `cqi` with maxima above what the reference asks
   for, and they all render at their maximum: the centre column's container
   (`retro-center`, declared on `.preview-panels`) only exists while the right
   panel is open, so `cqi` falls back to `preview-frame` — 1348px against the
   890px frame the values came from. A 34px-tall status icon beside a 15.7px
   line, a 44px tile on a 68px card, and a 22px chevron on a 16px label.
   So they hang off `--retro-icon` instead, which is this style's one icon
   size (17.6px at desktop) and already scales with the preview. */

/* The tool row's status mark.
   One token, square, at this style's own icon size — and the route here is
   worth keeping, because the first fix was to the wrong thing.

   Reported as "这个图标有点大了" over the file mark on 正在读取文件. It really
   did read large, so this was `calc(var(--retro-icon) * 0.8)` for a while. But
   the follow-up — "他底部没有展示全" — located the actual defect: the mark was
   not too big, it was the one glyph in the set drawn at the wrong scale.
   `RetroSheetIcon` kept its source file's coordinates, so it carried 19.18
   units of stroked height where every sibling has 16.18, overflowed its own
   `viewBox="0 0 19 19"` by 0.89 at the bottom, and had its whole bottom border
   clipped away. Shrinking it scaled the clipping down with it, which is exactly
   why that did not help.

   The glyph is refitted now (see `retroIcons.tsx`), so the size belongs back at
   `--retro-icon` where the rest of the row's marks already sit. **A CSS factor
   here would have been a permanent correction for a one-glyph drawing error**,
   and it would have mis-sized the other four file-tool marks to hide it.

   Still a token, and still square, because both of those were real: the holder
   was `0.88 × --retro-icon` wide against a square SVG at full size, so the
   glyph overflowed its container by 2.1px. The 0.88 dated from the exported
   `file-status.svg`, which genuinely was 30:34 — `retroIcons.tsx` draws the
   whole set on one square viewBox now and the holder never caught up. Both
   values were legal, which is why nothing caught it. One token, read twice on
   both axes, cannot drift again. */
.preview-frame[data-style-preset="retro"] .tool-card .tool-status-icon {
  --retro-status-icon: var(--retro-icon);
}
/* This one used to paint `/retro/file-status.svg` here and hide the icon
   underneath (`> * { display: none }`). That is the whole of "有的没有和中间栏
   关联上": the left rail's 查看 / 编辑 / 搜索 / 运行命令 galleries each set an
   icon slot, and on this style the row drew one fixed file mark whatever the
   reader picked — four galleries that did nothing.

   The mark itself was not the problem, so it is not lost: `RetroSheetIcon` is a
   path-for-path port of that file, and it is the first tile of 查看. What
   changed is that the row now renders the *pick*, and the whole set is drawn
   in the same hand (`retroIcons.tsx`) so any of the four still reads as this
   style. `currentColor` in place of its baked `#3A332B` is the other gain —
   the exported SVGs are why this style cannot have a dark colourway. */
.preview-frame[data-style-preset="retro"] .tool-card[data-file-tool="true"] .tool-status-icon {
  width: var(--retro-status-icon);
  height: var(--retro-status-icon);
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 0;
  background: none;
}

.preview-frame[data-style-preset="retro"] .tool-card .tool-status-icon > svg {
  width: var(--retro-status-icon);
  height: var(--retro-status-icon);
}

.preview-frame[data-style-preset="retro"] .artifact-launch-card .artifact-inline-icon {
  /* 1.8× the icon size: a tile, but not one that fills the card — at 44px it
     was taller than the two lines of text beside it put together. */
  width: calc(var(--retro-icon) * 1.8);
  height: calc(var(--retro-icon) * 1.8);
  background-color: var(--surface-inset);
  background-image: url("/retro/attachment-cube.svg");
  background-position: center;
  background-repeat: no-repeat;
  background-size: contain;
}

/* This one stays painted, and the distinction is the point: the box below holds
   three hardcoded spans (`Globe2`, the comic mark, and a `StateIcon`) of which
   CSS shows one, and outside 像素风 and 漫画风 the one shown is the globe. So
   there is no icon slot behind it in this style and no gallery it could be
   ignoring — unlike the tool row above, where hiding the child really did
   disconnect four galleries. Chrome, not a slot. */
.preview-frame[data-style-preset="retro"] .artifact-launch-card .artifact-inline-icon > * {
  display: none;
}

.preview-frame[data-style-preset="retro"] .artifact-action-open > svg {
